1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,572
About 1 in 3 adults in industrialized countries lives with gastritis — are you one of them?

2
00:00:04,892 --> 00:00:14,048
Gastritis means the stomach lining is inflamed, and its normal barrier against acid breaks down, so acid ends up irritating the exposed tissue underneath.

3
00:00:14,368 --> 00:00:16,526
Three everyday habits make that worse.

4
00:00:16,846 --> 00:00:18,366
First, drinking alcohol.

5
00:00:18,686 --> 00:00:26,642
Alcohol interferes with normal acid secretion and irritates the stomach lining directly, so acid attacks the very tissue meant to hold it back.

6
00:00:26,962 --> 00:00:28,175
Second, chronic stress.

7
00:00:28,495 --> 00:00:37,817
Ongoing stress reduces blood flow to the stomach lining while also increasing acid production — a combination that leaves the lining more exposed and slower to repair itself.

8
00:00:38,137 --> 00:00:39,146
Third, smoking.

9
00:00:39,466 --> 00:00:48,903
Nicotine travels through the bloodstream to the stomach, where it reduces protective mucus and blood flow to the lining while increasing acid production — weakening the lining's defenses from the inside.

10
00:00:49,223 --> 00:00:53,360
Cut back on alcohol and give your stomach real recovery time between drinks.

11
00:00:53,680 --> 00:00:59,069
Build small stress breaks into your day — even a few minutes of slow breathing can ease the acid response.

12
00:00:59,389 --> 00:01:03,629
And if you smoke, quitting is one of the most direct ways to protect your stomach lining.

13
00:01:03,949 --> 00:01:06,924
If pain keeps coming back, see a doctor to check for H.

14
00:01:07,244 --> 00:01:08,687
pylori infection too.
